          "source": "topic-set-paleontology-dinosaurs-101-🆔20251018203334.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Ontogenetic Niche Partitioning:** The study of how a dinosaur's ecological role (e.g., its prey) changed as it grew—for example, how a juvenile *T. rex* hunted different animals than its parents, effectively competing with smaller predators.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 107,
          "source": "topic-set-paleontology-dinosaurs-101-🆔20251018203334.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dinosaur Paleopathology:** The study of injuries and diseases in dinosaurs. Healed fractures, bite marks, and infections preserved in fossils provide powerful clues about their behavior and interactions.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 109,
          "source": "topic-set-paleontology-dinosaurs-101-🆔20251018203334.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The \"Warm-Blooded\" Debate:** An exploration of the evidence for **endothermy** (warm-bloodedness) in dinosaurs, including their rapid growth rates, bone histology, and predator-prey ratios.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 110,
          "source": "topic-set-paleontology-dinosaurs-101-🆔20251018203334.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Melanosome Preservation:** A cutting-edge field that analyzes preserved pigment-bearing organelles (melanosomes) in fossil feathers to reconstruct the *actual colors* of dinosaurs.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 111,
          "source": "topic-set-paleontology-dinosaurs-101-🆔20251018203334.md"
        }
      ]
    },
